Let the settings list and the modal editor shrink to a phone-width window.

On a 411px viewport the Settings editor, which opens as a modal, overflowed twice.

SettingsEditor2 keeps its list pane at 500px or wider, both as the editor's minimum width and
as the minimum of the split view that holds the list. On a phone the list was therefore 131px
(26%) wider than the screen and its right part, the controls and the end of every description,
sat off it.

ModalEditorPart lays the modal out at 80% of the window, centres it from that width, and then
resizableElement.layout raises the width to MODAL_MIN_WIDTH (400px). The left edge stayed where
the narrower width had put it, so the modal began at 41px and ended 30px past the right edge.

On Android the list may now shrink to 280px. NARROW_TOTAL_WIDTH, which decides when the table
of contents is dropped, still goes by 500px, so a tablet or a desktop-sized window lays out as
before. The modal's minimum width is capped at the window's, and the modal is centred from the
width it really gets.

